                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "how do the signals look from this?  It emits just the properties changed on the diffs?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "log_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 938,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Manish Tiwari",
                        "email": "tmanish.in+openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manishtwari"
                    },
                    "message": "In the current code, this does not emit any signals. I\u2019ll update the refresh path so only the properties whose values changed emit PropertiesChanged\nAt present, the properties expected to change are:\n1. resolved \n2. resolution (that is on the web UI so people can manually resolve a log)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "log_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 947,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "Why do we need this?\n\nDo we change severity after creating the event log? I don't think so, please correct me."
                },
                {
                    "file": "log_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 947,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Manish Tiwari",
                        "email": "tmanish.in+openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manishtwari"
                    },
                    "message": "You're right. Severity updates can happen during creation (via updateDBusSeverity()). When refreshFromDisk() deserializes, it gets the correct severity. This code is redundant will remove it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "log_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 949,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Arya K Padman",
                        "email": "aryakpadman@gmail.com",
                        "username": "aryakpadman"
                    },
                    "message": "And we can use std::list:remove(value) instead this lambda"
                },
                {
                    "file": "log_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 949,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "+1"
                },
                {
