                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "is it should be unique? \n\nWhat if we are trying to create two different temp dbus object?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "log_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 938,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Manish Tiwari",
                        "email": "tmanish.in+openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manishtwari"
                    },
                    "message": "No, there's no such case, even when multiple inotify events arrive in a batch, they're processed sequentially in the while loop. Each temp Entry object is created, used, and destroyed before the next event is processed.\nonly one temp object exists at any time, so using the constant tempId = 0xFFFFFFFF is safe."
                },
                {
                    "file": "log_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 938,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "ok"
                }
